												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Early Access Game</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">Get instant access and start playing; get involved with this game as it develops.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“In the current version of our game, we feel confident to present our game something more than a demo, but not yet a full game. We think it is the time to shift out of demo phase and start the next stage of bringing our work to our players.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“The current plan is for our game to stay in Early Access for a least a year as we work on making more content and refinement.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The full version will have more content compared to the Early Access, as we plan to introduce more missions, gears, perks, and items to the game. We are also planning to keep improving the structure of the game, and present a full experience.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The game's basic structures are nearly complete, but it still lack enough contents to make it a full game. At the start of Early Access, we will release the first 3 maps of the game with complete main missions and incomplete side missions, with numerous new items and improvements.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“The Early Access version will be released with a lowered price compared to the full version as this is not the full experience we would like our players to have. The full version will come at a raised price for there will be more content available. ”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“The community has always been an important part of our development process, we keep a close eye on the feedback and suggestions from our players, and these information is invaluable in help us improve our work.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
